      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A different structure of values and life frustrations was observed in subjects with psychosomatic disease than in healthy subjects. The subjects with ischemic disease were affected mostly in the sphere of working and existential needs, whereas their family and social relations were not disturbed, and they were not frustrated in the sphere of material needs, either. On the other hand subjects with ulcer disease felt much more affected in social relations and in primary material needs."},
